But in standard AES, [38;5;10mstate[0][0][0m should be XORed with [38;5;10mw[0][0] = 0x2b[0m and [38;5;10mstate[0][1][0m should be XORed with [38;5;10mw[1][0] = 0x28[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
So the C code's AddRoundKey is different from standard AES! In the C code, [38;5;10mrk[row][col] = w[base + row*4 + col][0m, but in standard AES, [38;5;10mrk[row][col] = w[base + col*4 + row][0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
